# Legacy UI is deprecated — do not extend it

The Jinja2 + HTMX dashboard at `src/twisted/engine/routes/web.py` and
`src/twisted/web/templates/**` is the **deprecated** Phase 5-7 UI.
Phase 8 replaced it with a React SPA at [`frontend/`](frontend/) and
the legacy surface only stays online to:

1. Serve the cookie-auth flow (`/login` GET+POST, `/logout`) that the
   SPA still consumes
2. Serve the screenshot redaction tool (`/dashboard/.../redact`) until
   an in-SPA redactor ships
3. Provide a fallback that operators with old bookmarks still find

## Rules for any change in this area

- **DO NOT add new `@router.get(...)` page handlers** to
  `src/twisted/engine/routes/web.py`. New UI pages go in
  [`frontend/src/pages/`](frontend/src/pages/) and get a route in
  [`frontend/src/App.tsx`](frontend/src/App.tsx).
- **DO NOT add new `.html` files** to `src/twisted/web/templates/`.
  Use [`frontend/src/components/`](frontend/src/components/) and
  shadcn primitives in `frontend/src/components/ui/`.
- **DO NOT add new HTMX fragment endpoints** (e.g. `hx-post=...`).
  Use TanStack Query mutations in the SPA instead.
- The CI guard in
  [`tests/integration/test_legacy_ui_guards.py`](tests/integration/test_legacy_ui_guards.py)
  enforces both counts (templates + GET routes). Adding to either side
  fails CI with an explanatory message.

## Acceptable edits to legacy files

- Removing a page (after porting it to the SPA) — lower the
  `EXPECTED_*` constants in the guard test to match.
- Bug fixes in the auth flow (`/login`, `/logout`).
- Bug fixes in the screenshot redactor.
- Banner / deprecation notice copy changes in `_base.html`.

## When in doubt

If the user asks for "a page that does X" or "a button that does Y" and
the natural place to put it is the legacy dashboard, push back: explain
that legacy is deprecated and propose the SPA equivalent. The SPA's
data + auth pipeline (TanStack Query + the `/api/*` endpoints + cookie
session) is identical to the legacy dashboard's, so functional parity
is always achievable.

The only acceptable exception is fixing an existing legacy bug while
the user is mid-task and doesn't have time to switch to the SPA.

## Off-switch

The `TWISTED_LEGACY_UI` env var (defined in
[`src/twisted/core/settings.py`](src/twisted/core/settings.py)) controls
the legacy surface:

- `enabled`  — legacy renders unchanged (no banner)
- `banner`   — legacy renders, every page shows "switch to SPA" banner
              (default)
- `disabled` — every legacy GET 307s to the SPA equivalent; POST
              endpoints (login, redact submit) still work

Operators who want a hard cutover set `TWISTED_LEGACY_UI=disabled`.
